      "content": "The Action-save path still calls `postSaveReview(binding.reviewDate)` without the saved Trade ID, so this new resume-from-Trade behavior only works for Debt resolutions. For example, when an earlier Trade is unfinished and the trader saves an Action on a later Trade that still owes a due reflection, the response jumps back to the earlier Trade instead of keeping the current Trade's reflection as the next task. Pass `binding.tradeId` from `attemptSave` as well so both save paths use the same continuation rule.",
